      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under N2, an ethanol solution (5 mL) of H4daps (43 mg, 0.1 mmol) was added to Dy(CF3SO3)3·6H2O (60 mg, 0.1 mmol) in ethanol (5 mL) and refluxed 3 h, then cooled to room temperature to give a bright yellow mother liquor. Excess acetic acid (29 μL, 5 equiv) was added, the mixture was stirred 10 min at room temperature and filtered, and diethyl ether vapor was diffused under N2. Light yellow rod-like crystals of 1Dy formed in a week.",
